# Netlify _redirects — SPA fallback + security headers
# All unknown paths fall back to index.html so React Router handles routing.
# Pre-rendered pages (/, /blog, /studio/*) are served as static HTML by Netlify
# automatically since vite-plugin-prerender writes them as real HTML files.

# Static assets — serve directly (no rewrite needed, Netlify handles these)
/mantram-logo.png           /mantram-logo.png           200
/mantram-logo.svg           /mantram-logo.svg           200
/mantram-favicon-32.png     /mantram-favicon-32.png     200
/mantram-favicon-192.png    /mantram-favicon-192.png    200
/dashboard-hero.png         /dashboard-hero.png         200
/sitemap.xml                /sitemap.xml                200
/robots.txt                 /robots.txt                 200
/llms.txt                   /llms.txt                   200

# SPA fallback — everything else gets index.html (React Router takes over)
/*    /index.html   200
